00:01:02.600 --> 00:01:06.137
Heather Mikulich: "What's
happening when my ears pop?

00:01:06.137 --> 00:01:08.010
"Nothing's actually popping, is it?"

00:01:08.010 --> 00:01:09.010
What you're probably feeling

00:01:09.010 --> 00:01:10.700
is your eustachian tube popping,

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:13.070
which is a very thin tube
that connects your sinuses

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.780
to your ear, and that tube
is actually quite small.

00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:17.280
So if you have pressure gradients

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.070
between your ear and your sinuses,

00:01:19.070 --> 00:01:21.080
especially if you're going up elevations,

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.280
that popping feeling is
just that eustachian tube

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.710
kind of releasing the pressure.

